        "file": "django/db/models/lookups.py",
        "start_line": 290,
        "end_line": 304,
        "side": "new",
        "severity": "medium",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "self.rhs iterated twice; one-shot iterables (generators) lose values",
        "explanation": "The new code reads self.rhs once in the any(...) check and again in either the ExpressionList comprehension or the prepared_values loop. The old code read it only once. If rhs is a one-shot iterator, such as filter(pk__in=(x for x in ids)), any() uses it up when it has no expressions. The loop then gets nothing, prepared_values is empty, and the In lookup matches nothing, so the query silently returns no rows. If an expression is present, any() stops at the first one, so every plain value before it is dropped from the ExpressionList. Query.resolve_lookup_value only rebuilds lists and tuples, so other iterables reach this method unchanged.",
        "suggestion": "Turn the iterable into a list once before checking it, e.g. `rhs = list(self.rhs)`, then use `rhs` in both the any() check and the loops (or assign self.rhs = rhs).",
        "evidence": "if any(hasattr(value, \"resolve_expression\") for value in self.rhs):",
        "confidence": 0.45,
